IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-types`
IMPORT `eia-dates`

-- Electricity Industry Act 2010 — GOAL 3: ENFORCEMENT.
--
--   "May the Authority still act on a Code breach; what is the most
--    pecuniary penalty; and by when must an appeal be lodged?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2010_116.txt — ss 52, 54,
-- 66, 80.

§ `Goal 3 — enforcement`

-- s 52 "(1) The Authority may not exercise its powers in relation to a breach
-- or possible breach of the Code if the breach— (a) was discovered, or ought
-- reasonably to have been discovered, more than 3 years before the exercise
-- of the power; or (b) occurred more than 10 years before the exercise of the
-- power. (2) However, once the Authority has exercised a power in relation to
-- the breach ..., the limitations in subsection (1) do not apply." "More than
-- 3 years before" day D: before D less 3 years (fork F2).
@ref s 52
@export Whether the Electricity Authority may still exercise its powers on a Code breach under s 52 of the Electricity Industry Act 2010 (NZ): not if the breach was (or ought to have been) discovered more than 3 years earlier, or occurred more than 10 years earlier — unless it has already exercised a power on that breach. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Code breach`  @desc When the breach occurred and was or ought to have been discovered, the day of the exercise, and any earlier exercise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may act on the breach` b IF
        b's `a power already exercised on the breach`
    OR  (    b's `breach discovered on` AT LEAST `add years` (b's `power exercised on`) (0 MINUS 3)
         AND b's `breach occurred on` AT LEAST `add years` (b's `power exercised on`) (0 MINUS 10))

-- s 54 "(1) ... (d) make a pecuniary penalty order ... of an amount not
-- exceeding $2 million and a further amount not exceeding $10,000 for every
-- day or part of a day during which the breach continues ... (3) Two or more
-- breaches relating to one event or series of closely related events arising
-- from the same cause or circumstance must be treated as a single breach."
@ref s 54(1)(d), (3)
GIVEN b IS A `Code breach`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most pecuniary penalty for the Code breach` b MEANS
    2000000 PLUS 10000 TIMES b's `days the breach continued`

-- s 80 "(2) The amount of any pecuniary penalty must not, in the case of an
-- individual, exceed $500,000 in respect of each act or omission. (3) ... in
-- the case of a body corporate, exceed ... the greater of— (a) $10 million;
-- or (b) either,— (i) if it can be readily ascertained and ... the
-- contravention occurred in the course of producing a commercial gain, 3
-- times the value of any commercial gain ...; or (ii) if the commercial gain
-- cannot be readily ascertained, 10% of the turnover of the body corporate and
-- all of its interconnected bodies corporate".
@ref s 80(2)-(3)
GIVEN p IS A `Part 3 contravener`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` p MEANS
    IF   p's `an individual`
    THEN 500000
    ELSE max 10000000 alternative
    WHERE
        alternative MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `commercial gain, if readily ascertained`
            WHEN JUST gain THEN IF p's `in the course of producing a commercial gain` THEN 3 TIMES gain ELSE 0
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.1 TIMES p's `turnover with interconnected bodies`

-- s 66 "An appeal under this Part must be made by giving notice of appeal
-- within 20 working days after the date of the decision or order appealed
-- against".
@ref s 66
GIVEN decided IS A DATE, matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal a decision of` decided `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the` 20 `th working day after` decided `, Matariki days` matariki
